now of course there's lots of talk about  emma radacano of course there is she is  the british teen tennis sensation  and she's back in bromley in london  after she starred in her very own fairy  tale in new york that's a cliche which  is getting old already  has to be said when she won the u.s open  just 18 years old not only that but the  first qualifier ever to win a grand slam  and managed to achieve that incredible  feat without losing a single  set well jackie has been talking to her  this morning  yeah it's a really nice feeling to be  home i have been able to spend some time  with my parents after not seeing them  for seven weeks so  we we just had a nice meal together last  night with some homemade dumplings and  uh i've re-watched the final just to  just to relive some experiences  and what was that like were you tense  re-watching the final  yeah i just really wanted to let the  moment sink in and i thought that would  help but um it i knew exactly what it  was going to happen in all of the points  but watching is definitely more  stressful than playing because you feel  like you have control at least when  you're playing when you're watching  um you you have no control and  but it was really cool to just be able  to  relive some of those moments and at the  end i i saw my slide when i fell and uh  it was quite long and i actually  impressed myself with that in slight  motion  it was a very impressive slide when you  saw your mum and dad for the first time  you know what did they say to you  because well played doesn't really cover  it does it  yeah they just gave me a hug there was  nothing really crazy they have very high  standards and uh tough love but i think  that i didn't really need anything big  from them i know that  just the smallest of congratulations  means a lot and for them to say they're  proud of me as well but they they were  very happy to have me home  life-changing experience emma you know  reporters paparazzi outside of your  house you are instantly recognizable  everywhere  are you ready for that how much your  life has now  changed yeah i actually haven't really  realized because i just came home and  i've just been staying at home spending  time with my family so i haven't really  gone out or done anything yet so i don't  really see at the moment any changes  well you've been super busy since that  match point you've done loads of things  at new york you've done chat shows  you've been to the met gala  well you looked fantastic um what was  the highlight of all those things that  you did because you won  thank you i think the highlight  of my time after the final was honestly  that night that of the final i just  spent it with my team in a really nice  intimate room and we just spoke about  the whole three weeks experience and  reflecting upon all the time uh there  was there was like a karaoke bus on the  way back from the courts when we were  singing sweet caroline and mr brightside  and we just had a really nice meal  together and discussed everything and  just chatted the whole time through  yeah and he's still going on adrenaline  because you were there for a very long  time you played 10 matches you've done a  lot of media afterwards you know are you  still on a high or you're starting to  feel a bit tired  yeah i think i'm still on a high when i  got home yesterday i just slept the  whole day so i think it's that i'm just  starting to recover and  rest and i think my body needs it after  the experience that i've had for the  last seven eight weeks andy murray  called obviously congratulated you  massively and he called it a great  opportunity  for british tennis what would it mean to  you if little girls and boys were  picking up a racket because of you  because you are their inspiration  yeah i mean it means a lot to to hear  that i think that  i want to just inspire you know little  girls or young children to to dream big  you know not even if it's not tennis if  it's other dreams like in in school  being a doctor or anything like that um  i just want to inspire them to dream big  and anything can happen but then also  for tennis i think it's  i just want to get across that you can  be a normal kid you can go to school  have all of the normal things and still  achieve  results and um i think that's that's my  main message to to all the kids out  there  it's a very sensible message as well  the liverpool manager jurgen klopp has  called you talent of the century he said  he was inspired by you he's now going to  watch a lot more women's tennis in the  future when you hear things like that  how does it make you feel  yeah i mean it's it's very very nice to  hear and i'm very grateful i think that  women's tennis at the moment is  extremely strong and the depth that the  game has um all of the players can  pretty much win every event and uh i'm  really grateful to mr jurgen klopp for  his comment  do you have a football team  i have i'm my football team is england  i'm not i'm not going into the actual  future  maybe it's maybe it should be liverpool  now um you are a bigger i know you're a  big f1 fan um you've always been a big  formula one fan the drivers have all  been talking about you lewis hamilton  said he was inspired by you and he  admired your focus and determination  um and you've been talking to him i  believe  yeah i mean i love formula one an  awesome and also motorsports i spoke to  lewis hamilton at the met gala and it  was really cool just to just to speak to  him and  after everything he's achieved he's such  a great inspiration  but in in formula one i mean i love  watching all the brits um you know lando  and uh georgia as well they they're all  they're all really cool to be flying  flying the flag high for for great  britain  and  he called it also  a dream it proves that dreams can come  true um does it still feel like a dream  has it properly sunk in yet what you've  achieved  gradually i think as time's passing you  you realize but it's funny because  sometimes  i'll just have random bursts where i'm  like oh my god i just won the us open  but then i'd  just go about normal and realize  nothing's happened and these bursts will  just come and go so it's a strange  feeling to comprehend but um how  watching the match last night helped  really let it sink in yeah and and going  back to your training at the lta it's  going to be a bit different you know you  are the british number one you're the  world number 23 you are a grand slam  champion people are going to treat you  differently you can't just go in and  train anonymously are you prepared for  that  honestly i can't even get a call at my  local club like it's still  but uh i haven't really even thought of  that when i when i go back to training  um i'll see if anything changes but  until then nothing  and you know more demands on your time  obviously  now you're a superstar are you prepared  for that  yeah i think it i won't over commit  myself i'll just uh  take it take it how it is and you know i  think the most important thing for me is  still my tennis and improving and  training so i i won't let any commitment  get in the way of that because it's my  top priority  but what now though you've achieved your  goal which is to win a grand slam at  your second attempt at the age of 18.  some people would say that's it that's  the pinnacle  my my goal now is just to keep improving  and maximize my potential and what i can  do it's pretty amazing because i feel  like even though i won the u.s open  there are still many many aspects of my  game that i feel could improve and get  better so  i'll probably after some time off  reflect on what's just happened and then  go and go about and see where i can  improve and start working on those and  you had so much support from all around  the world from  so many famous people did any of the  messages make you particularly  starstruck  i  haven't really read all my messages till  i'm just trying to  enjoy the moment and coming home i  wanted to just spend time with my family  and in new york it was a really busy but  amazing experience so over the next few  days i'm hoping to to really plow  through some of them and i'm sorry if i  haven't replied yet  but you got a congrats from the queen  didn't you  yeah i did i received a note from her  majesty and it meant a lot that  she would she was following  the matches and  um i'm just really honored and grateful  and i'll probably cherish that letter  forever yeah maybe frame it um was there  anything finally that you were really  looking forward to when when you came  home something you were looking forward  to doing sleeping your own bed or eating  something particular and whatever it was  have you done it  yeah i think sleeping in my own bed uh i  woke up this morning and i didn't know  where i was it was one of those like  where am i but i also  had a really nice meal homemade  dumplings by my mom i was craving them  so  getting a taste of home was very very  nice so i've done that
 

